   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 2,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "Why some numbers do nothing",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## The linked-widget trap\nThe numbers printed on `EmptyLTXVLatentVideo`, `LTXVEmptyLatentAudio`, `LTXVConditioning` and `CreateVideo` are **dead** - those inputs are driven by the green primitives through links. Editing them does nothing. Change **Stage-1 width / height, Frames and FPS** instead.\n\nRule for any workflow: if an input has a wire going into it, its widget value is ignored."
   ],
   "color": "#6b4e16",
   "bgcolor": "#8a6620"
  },
  {
   "id": 4,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    1540,
    -150
   ],
   "size": [
    430,
    240
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 3,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "Why the negative prompt is empty",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Negative prompt at cfg 1.0\nThe distilled model runs at video/audio cfg **1.0**. At cfg 1.0 the negative branch cancels out mathematically, so the negative prompt below has **no effect**. Raising cfg on the distilled model is not the fix either: we tested video/audio cfg 3.0/7.0 and the look got markedly worse, and real cfg evaluates two branches every step.\n\nControl the look with the **positive** prompt and the **seed**."
   ],
   "color": "#6b4e16",
   "bgcolor": "#8a6620"
  },
