   "widgets_values": [
    "A wide shot at blue hour of a narrow stone canal in an old harbour town. Tall narrow houses painted in faded ochre and teal line both banks, their lit windows reflecting as long trembling strokes of gold on the dark water. A single wooden rowing boat drifts slowly from the left edge toward the centre of the frame, a man in a navy wool coat pulling the oars in an unhurried rhythm, small ripples spreading behind the blades. The camera glides gently forward along the canal at walking pace, keeping the boat near the centre, and ends framed on the stone bridge ahead with its row of hanging lanterns. Cool blue sky, warm window light, a soft cinematic grade with gentle film grain. The audio is the slow knock and drip of the oars, water lapping against the stone walls, and a distant church bell; the soundtrack consists of these sounds alone."
   ],
